    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">To Wish on a Dandelion</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;"They moved." She looks at Catraâ€™s belly with what can only be adoration. Adora can almost imagine the little one in there. "You're already so talented, aren't you?" Adora loves this baby more than she ever thought sheâ€™d love anyone except for Catra. She canâ€™t wait to meet them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catraâ€™s hand grazes the side of Adoraâ€™s head, and it makes her shiver. "Adora, they are supposed to be moving by now."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She shakes her head, nuzzling Catraâ€™s belly. "Shhh, positive reinforcement is important." Her hand rests on the spot the baby bumped, hoping for another. "Besides, they gave me their first high five. I'm obviously their favorite aunt. Scorpia can eat my dust."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"Well, you're the aunt they are living with, so you sure have an advantage."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"Damn right, I have the advantage." Itâ€™s an odd place to be. Sheâ€™s painfully aware of the fact that this baby is just Catraâ€™sâ€”it doesnâ€™t help Adora feel any less attached. Sheâ€™s not sure that sheâ€™s able to hold back and she isnâ€™t willing to try. "And I'm going to press it."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;OR&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora's in love with her roommate who is having a baby. This is fine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Searching for Dandelion Wine Adora POV/Accidental Pregnancy AU&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
